ARM: dts: n8x0: TMP105 temperature sensor

The N800/N810 have a TMP105 on I2C1 at 0x48, next to Menelaus (as QEMU's
n800/n810 machines model them); Maemo's DSME watches it to power off at
a critical temperature. lm75 drives it as a hwmon device "tmp105".

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap2420-n8x0-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/ti/omap/omap2420-n8x0-common.dtsi
@@ -45,6 +45,12 @@
 &i2c1 {
 	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 
+	/* Board temperature, DSME's thermal shutdown (A0 grounded) */
+	temperature-sensor@48 {
+		compatible = "ti,tmp105";
+		reg = <0x48>;
+	};
+
 	pmic@72 {
 		compatible = "menelaus";
 		reg = <0x72>;
